@host = http://localhost:5163

### The catalog: books, videos and the three memberships
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products

### The demo customer before ordering: no memberships, no access
GET {{host}}/api/v1/customers/4567890

### Place the PDF's example order: the First Aid video, "The Girl on the train" and the Book Club membership
# @name placeOrder
POST {{host}}/api/v1/purchase-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 4567890,
  "productIds": [1, 2, 3]
}

### BR1: the Book Club membership is now active on the customer
GET {{host}}/api/v1/customers/4567890

### The order that was just placed, with the price each item had at the time
GET {{host}}/api/v1/purchase-orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### BR2: the shipping slip lists only the physical product (the book)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/purchase-orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}/shipping-slip

### A video and a membership need no shipping, so this order gets no slip
# @name digitalOrder
POST {{host}}/api/v1/purchase-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 4567890,
  "productIds": [1, 4]
}

### 404: no shipping slip for that order
GET {{host}}/api/v1/purchase-orders/{{digitalOrder.response.body.$.id}}/shipping-slip

### 422: product 99 does not exist
POST {{host}}/api/v1/purchase-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 4567890,
  "productIds": [1, 99]
}

### 400: an order needs at least one product
POST {{host}}/api/v1/purchase-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 4567890,
  "productIds": []
}
